## Tool Name: run_smbclient
### Description: Run smbclient to connect to an SMB/CIFS server and optionally execute commands.
Operations include things like getting files from the server to the local machine, putting files from the local machine to the server, retrieving directory information from the server and so on.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'target': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The target IP address or NetBIOS name.'}, 'service': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The name of the SMB service to connect to (e.g. the name of a share or a printer).'}, 'username': {'default': 'guest', 'type': 'string', 'description': 'The username for authentication. If not provided, defaults to "guest".'}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'The password required to access the specified service on the specified server. If not provided, no password will be used (\'-N\' for anonymous access). If empty string "", forces an empty password via \'user%\'. If a string is provided, uses that password.'}, 'command': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': 'ls', 'description': 'Semicolon-separated list of commands to be executed.'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Additional arguments for smbclient (e.g. '-p 139')."}, 'timeout': {'default': 120, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum time in seconds that the command is allowed to run for (default is 120 seconds).'}}, 'required': ['target', 'service'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_netexec
### Description: Run a netexec (nxc) command.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'protocol': {'enum': ['smb', 'ldap', 'ssh', 'ftp', 'wmi', 'winrm', 'rdp', 'vnc', 'mssql', 'nfs'], 'type': 'string', 'description': "The protocol to use for execution (e.g. smb, ldap). To view a protocols options, run: 'nxc <protocol> --help'"}, 'target': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The target IP address, hostname, CIDR, IP range or file containing a list of targets.'}, 'username': {'default': '', 'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional username for authentication.'}, 'password': {'default': '', 'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional password for authentication.'}, 'extra_args': {'default': '', 'type': 'string', 'description': "Additional command-line arguments to pass to nxc (e.g. '--shares' when enumerating shares through SMB)."}, 'timeout': {'default': 120, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum time in seconds that the command is allowed to run for (default is 120 seconds).'}}, 'required': ['protocol', 'target'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_nslookup
### Description: Run nslookup to query DNS records.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The domain name or IP address to query.'}, 'record_type': {'anyOf': [{'enum': ['A', 'AAAA', 'MX', 'NS', 'SRV', 'TXT', 'PTR'], 'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "DNS record type (e.g., 'A', 'AAAA', 'MX', 'NS', 'SRV', 'TXT', 'PTR')."}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Additional arguments for nslookup. (e.g. '_ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs.corp.local' or '_kerberos._tcp.dc._msdcs.corp.local')"}, 'timeout': {'default': 60, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum execution time in seconds.'}}, 'required': ['query'], 'type': 'object'}```

## Tool Name: run_kerbrute
### Description: Run kerbrute for Kerberos-based user enumeration and password spraying.
Modes:
    - 'userenum'     : Enumerate valid usernames. This does not cause any login failures so it will not lock out any accounts.
    - 'passwordspray': Spray a single password against many users. This will increment the failed login count and lock out accounts if used excessively.
    - 'bruteforce'   : Bruteforce passwords for users. This will increment the failed login count and lock out accounts if used excessively.
**Args Schema:** ```{'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'domain': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Target domain (e.g., 'corp.local')."}, 'dc_ip': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Domain controller IP address. If blank, will lookup via DNS.'}, 'mode': {'enum': ['userenum', 'passwordspray', 'bruteforce'], 'type': 'string', 'description': "Kerbrute mode ('userenum', 'passwordspray', 'bruteforce')."}, 'usersfile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Path to file containing usernames.'}, 'bruteforcefile': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': "Path to file containing username and password combinations (for bruteforce) in the format 'username:password'."}, 'password': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Single password (for passwordspray).'}, 'safe': {'default': False, 'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Enable safe mode (avoid account lockouts). When this option is enabled, if an account comes back as locked out, it will abort all threads to stop locking out any other accounts. Default: False.'}, 'extra_args': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None, 'description': 'Additional kerbrute arguments.'}, 'timeout': {'default': 300, 'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Max execution time in seconds. Default: 300 seconds.'}}, 'required': ['domain', 'dc_ip', 'mode'], 'type': 'object'}```

